eal  there was a popular theory within the  fandom that the second one for all user  might have been an older bakugou who  traveled back in time and the reason why  he had to travel back in time was to  make sure that the quirk one for all  is successfully passed from generation  to generation all the way down to deku  this theory was primarily inspired by  the second user's silhouette  which for a long time was the only  visual representation that we had  of the second user the silhouette showed  him as having a similar hairstyle to  bakugo  and the silhouette also appeared to show  him with similar gear to that of  bakugo's hero costume there was also a  side theory that the third one for all  user was actually kirishima  and that both bakuga and kirishima  travel to the past  together the recent face reveals  confirmed that the third user is  definitely not kirishima and while the  second user does have a passing  resemblance to bakugou  it is all but confirmed that it is not  him i know that some people are still  holding out hope that this  might be an older bakugo but to me it  seems clear that he is not  even though this particular theory about  time travel and boku no hero did not  pan out this whole thing made me wonder  does  some type of time traveling or time  manipulation exist  in mha or could it exist in the future  we know that many shonen series include  some sort of  op time manipulation ability including  black clover one piece dragon ball super  jojo's bizarre adventure wakfu and many  more and yes i did just name drop wakfu  because noximilian  is an amazing villain even mha itself  has already introduced  several quirks that are connected to  time or affect  time in some way even though they are  not capable of actual  time travel this includes chronostasis  a quirk that allows its user to slow  down the movements of anything or anyone  that he touches with his hair  sir nighti's quirk which allowed him to  see into someone else's future  and o