rys quirk doesn't allow for  time travel  then some other quirk could  theoretically make that happen  it could be an existing time-related  quirk that develops time travel  abilities  after it is artificially enhanced or  after it awakens  or it could be a quirk that is yet to  emerge sometime in the future  as a result of the quirk singularity  phenomenon  aries own quirk has already proven that  quirk singularity is very much  real and something similar could happen  again  this time with actual time travel a time  travel quirk that is too powerful to  control  could activate on its own maybe leading  to someone  accidentally being sent back in time or  forward in time  that one event could permanently change  the entire world of boku no hero  and become an entire new ark all on its  own  or it could be used as the plot for a  future non-canon movie that ends up  making a ton of money but doesn't affect  the main timeline so yes i do think that  a time traveling quirk or a quirk that  can manipulate time in some other  overpowered way  may already exist in mha and even if it  doesn't it  may appear in the future aries quirk  could evolve  into a time traveling quirk when it  awakens or an entirely new quirk could  appear  and develop such abilities but will this  actually happen in the story even if it  is technically  possible i honestly don't know because  whenever you introduce  time travel things can get complicated  quickly and of course  such an overpowered quirk could  potentially throw the entire power  scaling situation in boku no hero  completely out of whack  that is why using time travel in a  self-contained  semi-canon movie may be the best way to  go about it  whatever happens though time travel is  always an interesting concept  to think about and i personally love  stories that are able to handle time  travel  in an effective way but let me know what  you guys think do you agree with me that  time traveling or time manipulation  quirks are  possib